sycl: fuse Inkling's depth-attention mix into one kernel per token

HomeBrain patch on ggml-sycl. Applies on top of 0007.
Upstream tracking: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/32757

mix() attends over up to five stacked block outputs with learned queries:
RMS_NORM, a transposed copy, a REPEAT of the queries, two batched matmuls and
a softmax, two or three times per layer pass. The backend matches that
subgraph and runs one work-group per token, which reads the states twice and
stores nothing in between. More than 5 states or 4 queries run the ops as
before.

0006-0008 together, on an Arc Pro B60 with Inkling-2-Mini Q4_K_XL (ctx 131072,
q8_0 KV, -ub 512, warmed, against 0001-0005 in the same window, two rounds):
decode 19.9 -> 22.0 t/s, prefill 406 -> 454 t/s on an 847-token prompt and
389 -> 428 t/s on a 5.9K-token prompt.

